From 5520b388356b34ab81afff0a9ec4f34843c743a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:43:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Assembled stiffness matrix: pattern built for the nodes, then
 expanded

`batch::makeAssembledStiffnessMatrix` built the pattern of the local matrix
row by row for the degrees of freedom: for each row, the degrees of freedom
of its elements were marked, gathered and sorted. For the quadratic
tetrahedra of a polycrystal with 4.9 M unknowns per process, this took
about 12 s of one thread of the host at the first assembly of the tangent
operator, the GPU waiting (half of this assembly).

The degrees of freedom being the components of the nodes of the space, and
an element having all the components of its nodes, the pattern is the one
of the couplings between the nodes, each entry being a full block of
components. The pattern of the nodes is now built, with `vdim * vdim` times
fewer operations, then expanded: the columns of each row are written in
increasing order directly in the arrays of the matrix, the diagonal first.
The intermediate copy of the columns is no longer allocated.

The matrix is the same, bit for bit. The degrees of freedom of the elements
must be the ones of `computeElementsDegreesOfFreedom` (all the components
of the nodes of each element, component by component): others are refused.

GradientsKernelsTest: pattern compared to the one of MFEM for one, two and
three components numbered node by node or component by component, on
hexahedra, tetrahedra and quadrangles of orders 1 and 2; degrees of freedom
which are not the components of the nodes refused.
